      "notes": [
        "QLIN-02 is a shared curriculum-independent STACK question mapped directly to Ghana B9.2.1.1.1. It passed local validation, STACK testing, five-variant deployment, rendering, correct/partial/misconception grading, curriculum mapping, and live adaptive learner delivery.",
        "QLIN-03 is a shared curriculum-independent STACK procedural question mapped directly to Ghana B9.2.1.1.1. It passed STACK testing, five-variant deployment, diagnostic-distinctness checks, correct/partial/misconception grading validation, curriculum mapping, and live adaptive delivery through LR-01 -> QLIN-02 -> QLIN-03.",
        "QLIN-04 is a shared curriculum-independent STACK procedural question mapped directly to Ghana B9.2.1.1.1. It presents two linear relations in different algebraic forms and diagnoses the common sign error when rearranging ax+z=b. It passed authored tests, five-variant deployment, correct/partial/misconception grading validation, curriculum mapping, and live adaptive delivery through LR-01 -> QLIN-02 -> QLIN-03 -> QLIN-04.",
        "QLIN-05 is a shared curriculum-independent STACK visual question mapped directly to Ghana B9.2.1.1.1. It uses JSXGraph to plot two linear relations with four bound learner inputs and two PRTs. It passed authored tests, five-variant deployment, correct/partial/swapped-relation grading validation, alternative-valid-point validation, curriculum mapping, and live adaptive delivery through LR-01 -> QLIN-02 -> QLIN-03 -> QLIN-04 -> QLIN-05."
